{
 "_doc": "Food-intake wording (spec v1.8 10g.30). No intake metric exists, so a read that asks about food intake hands off (requested_metric_unavailable). Matching is case-insensitive on word boundaries, after the not_intake phrases are removed. always: intake wording on its own. with_calories: intake only next to a calorie word and with no burn word ('calories I've had today', 'calories I logged', 'diet' + calories). nutrients: intake with grams, via the patterns ({nutrients} is filled in); a how-much question names its own nutrients (not fat: \"how much fat I have\" is fat_mass). patterns: fixed phrases ('calories in' as the intake phrase, incl. 'calories (are) in a banana' and the ambiguous 'calories in a day/week' (10g.33 item 9: a burn verb or 'per day'/'a day' reads the typical-day trend instead); not 'calories in the last week' or 'in my workout'). intake_reads: the metrics an intake question is mis-planned as; intake wording anywhere in the request hands off a plan that reads one of them. Any other context sentence of an unrelated read is ignored (10g.28).",
